    "result_text": "Green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI agreed with the finding and moved the `selfLink` derivation to where its siblings live:\n\n- **Reverted** `model/Owner.java` \u2014 removed the `getSelfLink()` getter, so the JPA `@Entity` no longer hardcodes REST route layout.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", expression = \"java(owner.getId() == null ? null : \\\"/api/owners/\\\" + owner.getId())\")` on `toOwnerDto`, directly alongside the existing `displayName`/`initials` expression mappings. All three presentation-derived fields are now produced by the same mechanism.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 schema change kept as-is (the finding recommended keeping it).\n\nBehaviour is unchanged (same null-guard, same `/api/owners/{id}` output), the route-building concern now sits only in the REST/mapper layer, and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).",
