        "findings": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe `selfLink` derivation is placed in the wrong unit. It works (MapStruct auto-maps `owner.getSelfLink()` into the generated `OwnerDto.selfLink` because the property name matches), but it violates the layering and diverges from this codebase's established idiom.\n\n**Finding \u2014 presentation/routing logic lives on the JPA domain entity instead of the mapper.**\n\n- `Owner` (`model/Owner.java`) is the `@Entity` persistence/domain model. `getSelfLink()` hardcodes a REST URL structure (`\"/api/owners/\"`) into that entity. The domain model now knows about HTTP route layout \u2014 a concern that belongs at the edge, not in `model`. The project's own guidance stresses keeping DTO/response concerns at the edges and having steps in between work with entities.\n\n- The codebase already has a clear, consistent pattern for response-only derived fields on the `Owner`/`OwnerDto` schema. In `OwnerMapper`, both sibling fields are derived at map time:\n  ```java\n  @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(...)\")\n  @Mapping(target = \"initials\", expression = \"java(...)\")\n  OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n  ```\n  `selfLink` is exactly the same kind of field (readOnly, derived, not persisted) and should follow the same route \u2014 a third `@Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", expression = \"java(owner.getId() == null ? null : \\\"/api/owners/\\\" + owner.getId())\")` \u2014 rather than sprouting a getter on the entity. As written, three co-located derived fields are now produced by two different mechanisms, which a maintainer would not expect.\n\n- Duplication of the base path: `\"/api/owners/\"` already exists in `RespondWithOwnerCreated` (`URI.create(\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId())`). The new literal on the entity spreads that string to a third layer. Consolidating the derivation in the mapper (or a shared constant) keeps the route in the REST layer where the other copy lives.\n\nRecommended: revert the addition to `Owner.java` and add the `selfLink` derivation as an expression `@Mapping` in `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, alongside `displayName`/`initials`. Keep the `openapi.yml` schema change as-is."
